  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 363718488064
    m_Localized: <size=125%>What happens ? </size>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1
    m_Localized: The mechanism
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2
    m_Localized: Player objective
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3
    m_Localized: What should you do ?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4
    m_Localized: The adequate amount of <color=#50D500><b>glucose</b></color> is
      reestablished through the release of the <color=#50D500><b>glucagon hormone</b></color>,
      which it acts on liver cells where glycogen is stored, which is the reserve
      source of glucose in animals. Glucagon is produced in the pancreas in the form
      of a precursor protein, <color=#50D500><b>proglucagon</b></color>, and is stored
      in <color=#50D500><b>granules</b ></color> of certain cells in the <color=#50D500><b>pancreas</b></color>.
      Only when the blood sugar level drops, proglucagon is converted into glucagon,
      and this, secreted into the bloodstream, will act on the liver cells, triggering
      the mechanism that transforms glycogen into glucose.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5
    m_Localized: To normalize the sugar concentration in your blood, if it decreases,
      you must synthesize a proglucagon molecule and store it in a <color=#50D500><b>secretion
      granule</b></color>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6
    m_Localized: The immune system is composed of various cells, including <color=#50D500><b>macrophages</b></color>,
      present in the <color=#50D500><b>blood</b></color> and infected tissues. Foreign
      particles, such as viruses and bacteria, are engulfed by macrophages and then
      degraded with <color=#50D500><b>acidic hydrolase</b></color> enzymes contained
      in cellular organelles called <color=#50D500><b>lysosomes</b></color>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7
    m_Localized: The immune system is made up of several cells, including <color=#50D500><b>macrophages</b></color>,
      present in <color=#50D500><b>blood</b></color > and in different tissues of
      our body. When foreign particles, such as viruses, bacteria, fungi and others,
      penetrate the body, they are engulfed by macrophages and then degraded by the
      action of enzymes <color=#50D500><b>acid hydrolases</b></color>, contained
      in cellular organelles called <color=#50D500><b>lysosomes</b></color>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8
    m_Localized: 'Digestion converts most of the large quantity of <color=#50D500><b>carbohydrates</b></color>
      present in this diet into <color=#50D500><b>glucose</b></color>, a type of
      sugar that is the main <color=#50D500><b>energy source</b></color> for cellular
      <color=#50D500><b>metabolism</b></color>. However, free glucose in the bloodstream
      cannot enter some cells by itself and requires the <color=#50D500><b>hormone
      insulin</b></color> for that.

      The precursor of insulin is the protein
      <color=#50D500><b>proinsulin</b></color>, constantly produced and stored in
      <color=#50D500><b>granules within certain cell int the <color=#50D500><b>pancreas</b></color>.
      Moments after meals, proinsulin molecules are converted into insulin, secreted
      into the blood, and distributed to a large portion of the body''s cells through
      circulation.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9
    m_Localized: Synthesize a molecule of proinsulin and store it in a <color=#50D500><b>secretory
      granule</b></color> so that, after other meals like this one, it can be transformed
      into insulin and released.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10
    m_Localized: Melanin is produced in the Golgi apparatus of skin cells called
      <color=#50D500><b>melanocytes</b></color>. The continuous accumulation of melanin
      causes gradual darkening of the skin, increasing <color=#50D500><b>protection</b></color>
      against solar radiation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11
    m_Localized: To ensure the health of your skin, avoid strong sunlight, use sunscreen,
      and synthesize a molecule of <color=#50D500><b>tyrosinase</b></color>, an enzyme
      that catalyzes one of the synthesis reactions of melanin.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
